 With Unlike Denominators" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050131 #edb/ref 1033 2353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050131 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "2f4d3750-cf40-5c57-8c23-75261a047653" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1031 "Measures of Segments" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1033 1379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "53e39f98-0b09-5a55-8519-b9bae786a859" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063956 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13262" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063956 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the value of $0-(-6)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063956 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "18486b46-10bc-5e64-b1d9-df3ba0736b05" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063956 #edb/ref 1074 "To subtract $-6$ from $0$, we combine the two negative signs to make a single plus sign. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0 - (-6) &=  \\\\\n0 + 6 &=  \\\\\n&= 6 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/a7/a793deb0faa2f175a7f9bddc13dcff381b48aaee40b6082bd320a8748d8c8c37.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063957 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13263" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063957 #edb/ref 1071 "Subtract $-100$ from $-85$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063957 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1c75cfa3-630e-5b37-82c0-ec421bb8c206" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063957 #edb/ref 1074 "To subtract $-100$ from $-85$, we combine the two negative signs to make a single plus sign. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-85 - (-100) &=  \\\\\n- 85 + 100 &=  \\\\\n&= 15 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063958 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13264" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063958 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $-3-(-1.5)$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063958 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "735b7c5c-68c6-51b9-b3c0-cc38a4e59e95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063958 #edb/ref 1074 "To subtract $-1.5$ from $-3$, we combine the two negative signs to make a single plus sign. This gives\n\n$$\n-3 - (-1.5) =-3 + 1.5\n$$\n\nTo calculate $-3+1.5$, we start at $-3$ and move $1$ place to the right. Then, we move another $0.5$ places to the right:\n\n![](images/f8/f8ebeccc7db234acc592ffd79aeeb92ce5ce5a756c4500019a1c5316f78d640d.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-3-(-1.5)= -1.5\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063959 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13265" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063959 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $\\dfrac{3}{7} - \\left(-\\dfrac{11}{7} \\right)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063959 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "347baa8c-4ba0-559a-a5b6-81e024054af6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186063959 #edb/ref 1074 "To subtract\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{11}{7}\n$$\n\nfrom\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{7}\n$$\n\nwe combine the two negative signs to make a single plus sign. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{7} - (-\\frac{11}{7}) &= \\frac{3}{7} + \\frac{11}{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a common denominator of $7$, so we combine numerators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{7} + \\frac{11}{7} = \\frac{3 + 11}{7} = \\frac{14}{7}\n$$\n\nNow, we can simplify the resulting fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{14}{7} &= 14 \\div 7 = 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** If two fractions have different denominators, we need to put them over a common denominator first and *then* add or subtract!" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064350 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/re